 oak grove at admission-free Bonnet Springs Park.","notes":"Pause at overlooks, scan the canopy for wildlife, and keep the group together without blocking the elevated walkway.","short_summary":"An elevated social walk through the tree canopy in Bonnet Springs Park.","evidence_claim":"Bonnet Springs Park’s current FAQ names the Crenshaw Canopy Walkway and confirms that the park charges no admission except where noted for special events.","source_url":"https://bonnetspringspark.com/frequently-asked-questions/","source_title":"Frequently Asked Questions","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Enter during park gate hours; attractions can have narrower operating windows. Pets are not permitted on the walkway.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kiwanis-cares-kids-treehouse","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Kiwanis Cares for Kids Treehouse","title":"Meet Up at the Kiwanis Treehouse","subtitle":"Explore an accessible raised treehouse inside Bonnet Springs Park.","notes":"Use the treehouse as a group meetup, explore its elevated setting, and yield space if a scheduled program is underway.","short_summary":"A playful, admission-free gathering point raised among the park’s oak trees.","evidence_claim":"Bonnet Springs Park’s FAQ identifies the Kiwanis Cares for Kids Treehouse and states that general park admission is free unless noted for special events.","source_url":"https://bonnetspringspark.com/frequently-asked-questions/","source_title":"Frequently Asked Questions","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"General park entry is free; the treehouse may be unavailable during reservations or programs. Pets are not permitted inside.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"givewell-nature-center","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"GiveWell Community Foundation Nature Center","title":"Compare Notes at the Nature Center","subtitle":"Study local plants, animals, and water systems inside Bonnet Springs Park.","notes":"Pick one exhibit theme per person, then regroup outside and explain one surprising ecological connection you noticed.","short_summary":"A collaborative nature-learning stop within Lakeland’s admission-free urban park.","evidence_claim":"The park FAQ identifies the Nature Center as a staffed park building and confirms that Bonnet Springs Park does not charge general admission.","source_url":"https://bonnetspringspark.com/frequently-asked-questions/","source_title":"Frequently Asked Questions","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The Nature Center’s interior is available only when staff are present; general park entry remains free.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lakeland-regional-health-circulator","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"Lakeland Regional Health Circulator","title":"Walk or Roll the Circulator","subtitle":"Follow Bonnet Springs Park’s marked shared route at an easy group pace.","notes":"Choose a turnaround point before starting, follow posted speed limits, and use the route’s distance markers to track progress.","short_summary":"A free marked route for a conversational walk, run, or low-speed ride around the park.","evidence_claim":"Bonnet Springs Park confirms that low-speed cycling is allowed on the Circulator, that it has distance markers, and that park admission is free.","source_url":"https://bonnetspringspark.com/frequently-asked-questions/","source_title":"Frequently Asked Questions","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the Circulator during gate hours and obey posted speed limits; wheeled devices are restricted from smaller paths and boardwalks.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"bonnet-springs-storywalk","subject_type":"activity","entity_name":"StoryWalk at Bonnet Springs Park","title":"Read the StoryWalk Together","subtitle":"Follow book pages along a nature path near the Crenshaw Canopy Walk.","notes":"Take turns reading each sign aloud, pause to notice nearby nature details, and let faster groups pass between pages.","short_summary":"A self-guided combination of shared reading, light walking, and outdoor observation.","evidence_claim":"Bonnet Springs Park describes StoryWalk as a self-guided walk with book pages along a path and lists the host park as open with free admission.","source_url":"https://bonnetspringspark.com/education/storywalk-at-bsp/","source_title":"StoryWalk at BSP","source_kind":"business_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The StoryWalk page lists park gates from 6:00 AM to 8:00 PM; participation uses the posted signs and requires no purchase.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
